</section>

<!-- ================= PROJECTS ================= -->
<section id="projects">
  <div class="tag">~/portfolio</div>
  <h2><span class="n">01.</span>Security Tooling</h2>
  <p style="color: var(--muted); max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: 1.8rem;">
    A coherent toolkit I designed, built, and tested end-to-end — each repo is a
    working, zero-dependency Python security tool with a real test suite.
  </p>
  <div class="grid">

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">📡</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/netrecon" target="_blank" rel="noopener">netrecon</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>Async TCP port scanner with service fingerprinting and banner grabbing. 500 concurrent connections, 60+ service signatures, JSON/CSV export.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">asyncio</span><span class="chip">recon</span><span class="chip">17 tests</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/netrecon" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">🎣</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/phishguard" target="_blank" rel="noopener">phishguard</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>Static phishing URL detector — 30+ lexical heuristics: brand spoofing, IDN homoglyphs, credential-bait keywords. Scores any URL 0–100, fully offline.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">heuristics</span><span class="chip">OSINT</span><span class="chip">21 tests</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/phishguard" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">🔓</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/hashbreak" target="_blank" rel="noopener">hashbreak</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>Hash identification for 18+ formats, rule-augmented dictionary cracking with salt support, and offline password strength auditing.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">crypto</span><span class="chip">audit</span><span class="chip">27 tests</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/hashbreak" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">📊</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/logsentinel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">logsentinel</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>SSH/auth log intrusion analysis: brute-force bursts, password-spray campaigns, and the alert that matters — successful logins after failed ones.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">SIEM</span><span class="chip">blue team</span><span class="chip">16 tests</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/logsentinel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">📜</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/certwatch" target="_blank" rel="noopener">certwatch</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>TLS certificate watchdog: expiry countdown, self-signed detection via CA validation, weak-key flags, wildcard-aware hostname/SAN matching.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">TLS</span><span class="chip">x509</span><span class="chip">live-tested</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/certwatch" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">🔎</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/redact" target="_blank" rel="noopener">redact</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>Secret scanner with 20+ credential rules — AWS keys, GitHub tokens, PEM blocks, DB URIs — entropy-filtered, with in-place auto-redaction.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">CI gate</span><span class="chip">regex</span><span class="chip">17 tests</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/redact" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">🛡️</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/sysarmor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">sysarmor</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>Linux hardening auditor: CIS-style checks on SSH config, permissions, sysctl, accounts — scores a host 0–100 with per-check remediation.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">CIS</span><span class="chip">hardening</span><span class="chip">16 tests</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/sysarmor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">🇵🇭</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/ulatbayan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UlatBayan</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>Barangay complaint & reporting system — full-stack civic app in one file, zero dependencies. Residents file & track reports; officials triage behind PBKDF2 auth; public transparency board shows the community what's being done.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">civic-tech</span><span class="chip">fullstack</span><span class="chip">CSRF/XSS-hardened</span><span class="chip">18 e2e tests</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/ulatbayan" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-head">
        <div class="card-icon">🌦️</div>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/Weather-App-Baler" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Weather App (Baler)</a></h3>
      </div>
      <p>Localized weather forecasting platform integrating real-time OpenWeather API streams — won <b>Best Innovation Award</b> at its competition debut.</p>
      <div class="chips"><span class="chip">HTML/CSS/JS</span><span class="chip">REST API</span><span class="chip">award-winning</span></div>
      <div class="card-links"><a href="https://github.com/Diavolo148888/Weather-App-Baler" target="_blank" rel="noopener">→ repo</a></div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= EXPERIENCE ================= -->
<section id="experience">
